Skip chunk load/unload Bukkit work when nothing is listening.

Four sites, all on the chunk load/unload path - which is one of the highest-frequency operations on
any server with players moving around.

1. CraftEventFactory#callEntitiesLoadEvent and #callEntitiesUnloadEvent stream every entity in the
   chunk through Entity::getBukkitEntity and collect them into a new list, then build a CraftChunk
   and an event. getBukkitEntity() *creates* the CraftEntity wrapper when one does not exist yet,
   so this was forcing wrapper allocation for every entity in every chunk that loaded. Both methods
   return void, so with no listener all of it is built and discarded.

2. LevelChunk#loadCallback built a CraftChunk and fired ChunkLoadEvent, which is notification-only.
   The CraftChunk is otherwise needed only by the populator path below it, so it is now created
   lazily and reused there if that path runs.

3. LevelChunk#unloadCallback built a CraftChunk and a ChunkUnloadEvent purely to read
   isSaveChunk() back off it. The event is constructed with saveChunk = true and only a listener
   can call setSaveChunk(), so with no listener isSaveChunk() is definitively true and mustNotSave
   is definitively false. The guarded branch sets that directly.

   This one is worth being explicit about because getting it wrong would mean chunks silently not
   saving. Verified two ways: the equivalence above is a proof rather than an assumption, and a
   build with these patches produces byte-for-byte the same world output as build 21 without them,
   including after an explicit save-all.

--- a/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/event/CraftEventFactory.java
+++ b/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/event/CraftEventFactory.java
@@ -2082,6 +2082,9 @@
     public static void callEntitiesLoadEvent(Level level, ChunkPos pos, List<Entity> entities) {
+        if (EntitiesLoadEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0) {
+            return;
+        }
         List<org.bukkit.entity.Entity> bukkitEntities = entities.stream().map(Entity::getBukkitEntity)...

@@ -2088,6 +2091,9 @@
     public static void callEntitiesUnloadEvent(Level level, ChunkPos pos, List<Entity> entities) {
+        if (EntitiesUnloadEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0) {
+            return;
+        }
         List<org.bukkit.entity.Entity> bukkitEntities = entities.stream().map(Entity::getBukkitEntity)...

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/LevelChunk.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/LevelChunk.java
@@ -722,2 +722,8 @@
-            org.bukkit.Chunk bukkitChunk = new org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftChunk(this);
-            server.getPluginManager().callEvent(new ChunkLoadEvent(bukkitChunk, this.needsDecoration));
+            org.bukkit.Chunk bukkitChunk = null;
+            if (ChunkLoadEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0) {
+                bukkitChunk = new org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftChunk(this);
+                server.getPluginManager().callEvent(new ChunkLoadEvent(bukkitChunk, this.needsDecoration));
+            }
@@ -735,0 +741,1 @@
+                if (bukkitChunk == null) bukkitChunk = new org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftChunk(this); // populators need it

@@ -755,5 +762,10 @@
+        if (ChunkUnloadEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0) {
+            this.mustNotSave = false;
+        } else {
         org.bukkit.Chunk bukkitChunk = new org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftChunk(this);
         ChunkUnloadEvent unloadEvent = new ChunkUnloadEvent(bukkitChunk, true);
         server.getPluginManager().callEvent(unloadEvent);
         this.mustNotSave = !unloadEvent.isSaveChunk();
+        }
